ros-jazzy-ros2-medkit-fault-reporter (0.7.1-1noble) noble; urgency=high

  * Delivery of a report is confirmed, and a report without a response is sent again. ``fault_reporter.delivery.ack_timeout_sec`` sets how long a response is awaited, a queued report is dropped after ``fault_reporter.delivery.max_attempts`` (10) tries, and a new report is dropped when ``fault_reporter.delivery.max_pending`` (1024) reports are queued. A report made while the service is not ready is dropped. When a reporter is destroyed, the ROS context takes its pending reports and keeps sending them (#764 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/764>)
  * **Breaking (ABI):** the member layout of ``FaultReporter`` in ``fault_reporter.hpp`` changed (``filter_`` is gone; ``delivery_config_``, ``delivery_`` and ``core_`` are new), so a binary built against 0.7.0 must be rebuilt. The reporting logic is split into a ROS-free core (#739 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/739>)
  * Contributors: @bburda

 -- "mfaferek93" <michal.faferek@selfpatch.ai>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0000

ros-jazzy-ros2-medkit-fault-reporter (0.7.0-1noble) noble; urgency=high

  * ``FaultReporter`` can now be constructed from an ``rclcpp_lifecycle::LifecycleNode`` (and from a plain ``rclcpp::Node`` reference or explicit node interfaces), enabling use inside lifecycle nodes (#556 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/556>, #555 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/issues/555>)
  * Build and test only: the package is instrumented for coverage (#582 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/582>), and every test takes a DDS domain at run time from the shared allocator (#551 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/551>, #597 <https://github.com/selfpatch/ros2_medkit/pull/597>)
  * Contributors: @bburda, @mfaferek93, @zeerekahmad

